// The `{` of a member never closed, and the `{` of its `impl`: the member is the innermost, and the `impl` ends at the same place, so it is not reported twice (N6).
// The unit is the last one of the file, so it ends at the end of the file. A bracket that is not closed is reported whatever
// stopped the reading: the E0002 points at the innermost bracket that is not closed (§18.1, S-943, R-371). The same file
// with an item after the unit is unclosed_next_n06_member_and_impl.onsa, and the report is on the same line.

